**Assessment:**

* The patient has chondromalacia of the patella, likely caused by overuse from swimming breaststroke.

**Plan:**

* The patient will take 600mg of ibuprofen four times a day with food to manage pain and inflammation.
* The patient will perform straight leg raising exercises to strengthen the quadriceps.
* The patient will avoid activities that put extra pressure on the knees, including breaststroke, and consider alternative swimming strokes that do not involve bending the knees.
* The patient will be followed up in a couple of weeks to reassess the condition.
* The patient's depression treatment will remain unchanged, and the patient will continue to attend therapy and engage in outdoor activities.
* The patient's carpal tunnel condition will be monitored and no changes will be made at this time.<|eot_id|>
