The physical examination reveals significant effusion of the right knee. There is a slight bit of ecchymosis. There is pain to palpation over the medial joint line. He is able to flex to 90 degrees, but there is pain at the end of the motion. He is able to extend to 115 degrees, but there is pain at the end of the motion. He has a positive Lachman's test.

Given the nature of his injury, I have ordered an MRI of the right knee to evaluate the integrity of the anterior cruciate ligament. The patient will follow up with me in 1 week to discuss the results of the MRI. I have recommended that he wear a knee immobilizer and use crutches when walking. I have also recommended that he limit his activities, including jogging. I have prescribed meloxicam 50 mg once daily. I have advised him to ice the knee if he is still swollen and in pain.

INSTRUCTIONS

Follow up in 1 week to discuss the results of the MRI. }}<|eot_id|>
