ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

1. Right elbow pain.
Medical Reasoning: The patient presents with a 4-day history of right elbow pain. She reports that she is a potter and has been working extensively on a ceramic bowl for her son's birthday. She denies any trauma. Her pain is worse with flexion and pronation. Her x-rays are unremarkable. Given her symptoms and exam findings, the diagnosis of medial epicondylitis is made. She will be placed in a sling for comfort and instructed to apply ice to the elbow for 20 minutes, 3 times a day. She will take 600 mg of ibuprofen every 6 hours as needed for pain, up to a maximum of 2400 mg per day. She will refrain from pottery for the next 2 weeks to allow the elbow to heal. We will refer her to physical therapy if her symptoms do not improve.
