summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Right elbow pain.

SOCIAL HISTORY

Patient reports that he is a father of two children, 13 and 10 years old, and that his 13-year-old son plays lacrosse. He has been playing lacrosse with his son for the past week, and he reports that he was hit in the right elbow during this time. He denies falling. He states that he has been playing with his children and thinks he is getting too old for this. He states that he has hurt himself before. He reports that his son got pretty rough with him and was checking him several times with a sick. He denies taking any medications for his pain.

MEDICAL HISTORY

Patient reports that he has a past medical history of hypertension and diabetes. He is currently on lisinopril 20 mg daily and metformin 500 mg daily. He states that he is compliant with his medications. He reports that he has been trying to reduce his salt intake and has been eating a Mediterranean diet. He denies eating fast food. He states that he has been taking his medications as prescribed. He denies any chest pain or shortness of breath.

VITALS

Blood pressure was 150/90 mmHg. Blood glucose was not checked.

PHYSICAL EXAM

Constitutional: In general appearance well-nourished.
CV: Grade 2/6 systolic ejection murmur.
Respiratory: Lungs are clear bilaterally.
Neurological: No focal neurological deficits.
Musculoskeletal: Examination of the right elbow reveals pain to palpation of the olecranon area of the posterior elbow. Mild pain with flexion and extension of the right elbow. Normal range of motion of the right elbow.

RESULTS

X-ray of the right elbow was reviewed and was normal.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Right elbow contusion.

Patient is a 54-year-old male who presents with right elbow pain. He reports that he was hit in the right elbow during a game of lacrosse with his son. He denies any fall. He reports that his son got pretty rough with him and was checking him several times with a sick. He denies taking any medications for his pain. He reports that he has been playing with his children and thinks he is getting too old for this. He reports that he has hurt himself before. He states that he has been taking ibuprofen and that it has helped. He reports that he has been icing his elbow. He reports that he has been trying to reduce his salt intake and has been eating a Mediterranean diet. He denies eating fast food. He states that he has been taking his medications as prescribed. He denies any chest pain or shortness of breath.

I have reviewed the patient's radiographic findings and he has a normal x-ray of his right elbow. His examination of his right elbow reveals pain to palpation of the olecranon area of the posterior elbow. Mild pain with flexion and extension of the right elbow. Normal range of motion of the right elbow. He is currently on lisinopril 20 mg daily and metformin 500 mg daily. He is compliant with his medications.

I have recommended that he continue to take ibuprofen 800 mg twice daily for the pain. I have also recommended that he ice his elbow three times a day for 20 minutes at a time. I have advised him to avoid playing lacrosse for the next couple of weeks to allow his elbow to heal. I have also recommended that he continue to follow up with his diabetes and hypertension.

Patient understands and agrees with the recommended plan. }}<|eot_id|>
