summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Acute on chronic CHF exacerbation.

SOCIAL HISTORY

Patient reports that he enjoys watching football and attending parties on the weekends, which he feels is the main reason for his diet slips.

MEDICATIONS

Patient reports that he is taking his medications most of the time but occasionally misses a dose or two.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Cardiovascular: Reports dyspnea.
• Respiratory: Denies dyspnea.
• Renal: Denies hematuria or changes in urinary habits.
• Gastrointestinal: Reports diet slips.
• Musculoskeletal: Denies muscle weakness.

VITALS

• Blood Pressure: 200/90.
• Oxygen Saturation: 99%.
• Respiratory Rate: 26.
• Heart Rate: 79.

PHYSICAL EXAM

• Neck: No jugular venous distention.
• Cardiovascular: 2/6 systolic ejection murmur, stable.
• Respiratory: Lungs are clear bilaterally.
• Musculoskeletal: Trace edema of the lower extremities.

RESULTS

Echocardiogram: Preserved EF of 55%, abnormal diastolic filling, and mild to moderate mitral regurgitation.

ASSESSMENT

• Congestive heart failure.
• Hypertension.
• Stage 3 chronic kidney disease.

PLAN

Patient will continue Bumex 2 mg daily and Norvasc 5 mg once daily. He will follow a low-sodium diet and avoid salty foods. He will weigh himself daily and contact the provider if he gains 3 pounds in 2 days. He will also follow up with a nutritionist for education on what foods he can eat. A renal artery ultrasound is recommended to rule out secondary causes of his kidney disease. }}<|eot_id|>
