PHYSICAL EXAM

• Respiratory: Auscultation of Lungs: Clear bilaterally. No wheezes, rales, or rhonchi.

RESULTS

Pulmonary function tests were reviewed and compared to previous results. The patient's pulmonary function test today is essentially unchanged from the 2019 results. Her FEV1 is 93% of predicted, FEV1/FVC is 81%, and her FEF 25–75 is 83% of predicted.

ASSESSMENT

• Asthma.
• Allergic rhinitis.
• Food allergy.

PLAN

The patient was advised to continue using her Wixela once a day. We discussed the option of stepping down to an inhaler that only has one medication in it, alvesco. We discussed the option of using the alvesco only when she is ill or during smoke season. We will repeat pulmonary function tests in 4 months to assess her progress. We will also repeat pulmonary function tests if she joins the military.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up in 4 months with pulmonary function testing. }}<|eot_id|>
