summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Bilateral upper quadrant pain.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Bobby Taylor is a pleasant 62-year-old male who presents to the clinic today for the evaluation of pain in the right upper quadrant. The onset of his pain began several weeks ago. The patient was referred by Dr. Miller who performed an ultrasound of the abdomen and found gallstones. He was advised to avoid fatty foods. He reports that he has not noticed any improvement in his symptoms. He has experienced nausea and low-grade fevers but has not vomited.

The patient is a type 2 diabetic and was advised to control his diabetes with diet and exercise. He has lost 25 pounds over the past 3 months and has been following a keto diet. He has noticed improvement in his blood sugar levels.

