Bobby Taylor is a 62-year-old male who presents today with bilateral upper quadrant pain. The onset of his pain began several weeks ago. The patient was referred by Dr. Miller who performed an ultrasound of the abdomen and found gallstones. He was advised to avoid fatty foods. He reports that he has not noticed any improvement in his symptoms. He has experienced nausea and low-grade fevers but has not vomited.

