I have had a lengthy discussion with the patient today regarding his right knee pain. I have explained to him that his examination is consistent with an anterior cruciate ligament tear. I have recommended that we obtain an MRI of the right knee to further evaluate the integrity of the ACL. I have also recommended that he take meloxicam 50 mg once a day. I have advised him to ice the right knee if he is still experiencing pain and swelling. I have recommended that he wear a knee immobilizer and use crutches when walking. I have advised him to limit his activities, including jogging. I have advised him to continue to work sitting at a desk. I have also advised him to avoid jogging until we get the results of his MRI.

