Julia Rodriguez is a 65-year-old female who presents for follow up after an interior STEMI.

The patient reports she was doing well after her last heart attack until she had an episode of chest pain that did not resolve after 20 minutes. She went to the emergency room and was diagnosed with an interior STEMI, and had another stent placed. She denies chest pain or shortness of breath.

She reports she saw me 6 months ago and was doing well at that time. She states she has been walking her dog 1.5 to 2 miles daily. She is excited for fall and has plans to see family and enjoy the weather. She notes she has noticed lower extremity edema since discharge from the hospital. She denies lower extremity pain. She states she is able to lie flat at night but may sit up a bit. She is able to afford her medications and is taking them as prescribed. She denies dietary changes, but notes she loves pizza and tries.

PAST HISTORY

Medical
Coronary artery disease.
Hypertension.
Diabetes.

SOCIAL HISTORY

Patient reports she walks her dog daily.

MEDICATIONS

Aspirin 81 mg daily.
Brilinta 90 mg twice daily.
Lipitor 80 mg daily.
Toprol 50 mg daily.
