Kyle Smith is a 34-year-old male who presents to the clinic today for the evaluation of low back pain. The onset of his pain began 2 weeks ago when he was lifting a box of books. He states that he heard a pop in his back at the time. The pain is located in the low back and is described as achy and sharp. He initially did not have pain radiating into his left leg, but now notes that it has started to radiate into his left leg. The pain is not exacerbated by any specific position. The patient states that he has tried taking ibuprofen and Tylenol for pain relief.

The patient denies any numbness or tingling in his left leg. He denies any loss of strength or loss of control of his bowel or bladder. The patient denies any history of spine conditions in his family. He does note that his father has back pain. The patient does not smoke. He has a history of playing soccer.

SOCIAL HISTORY

