After reviewing the patient's examination and radiographic findings today, we discussed treatment options. I have recommended a lumbar epidural steroid injection under fluoroscopy with a strong NSAID and a corticosteroid. This should help with the inflammation that is causing his pain. I explained the procedure in detail and the risks associated with it. We discussed that this is a typical procedure that I do all the time in-office. He will have the procedure today. }}<|eot_id|>
