Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) with functional abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Ms. Brittany Edwards is a 32-year-old female who was last seen in August 2019 with flares of abdominal pain, who was diagnosed with irritable bowel syndrome, or IBS, and was treated with Bentyl. She had a previous prescription for Reglan that she received from the emergency room that she used as needed for nausea. She was instructed to start a low dose fiber supplement, such as Citrucel, daily, probiotics to help with gas and bloating, Bentyl up to four times daily for intestinal cramping, and stop Reglan and use Zofran as needed. Neuromodulators such as Elavil and Buspar were discussed but not started.

The patient reports that she has been going out to eat on Friday nights and Saturday nights and that she has had some spicy foods or spicy shrimp. She notes that her gut does not always appreciate that. She reports that she is starting to notice that she is having bowel movements between 2 and 3 times a day. She reports that they are formed. After she has gone out either drinking with her friends, she tends to have more diarrhea. She states that it is the food or the alcohol, or both. She notes that she usually eats pasta at Friday's restaurant, and she always eats the chicken alfredo. She notes that it normally does not bother her. However, she does admit that it can make her bloated. She states that she usually drinks tequila or dark liquor, and she prefers Patron, but if she gets brown liquor, she only gets two. She notes that she drinks a martini every now and then. She notes that it is the mixer that they put in the drinks that she tends to put in the drinks. She states that she has had some luck using the fiber like Citrucel regularly.

She reports that she is still having cramping and sharp pains, so she has been avoiding heavy foods. She notes that she had some fried chicken today, though. She notes that it was fine. She notes that she cannot go without some fried chicken at least once in a while.

PAST HISTORY

Medical
Previous diagnosis of irritable bowel syndrome.

SOCIAL HISTORY

The patient reports that she is a social drinker.

