The patient reports that she is struggling with not drinking. She wanted to discuss this further, but we did not get to discuss it too much at her last visit. She states she last had a drink on Monday. She has gone a couple days without drinking. She has been drinking for a while. She reports drinking 4 to 5 times a week of hard alcohol. She states she is only taking half of the lisinopril. She reports she felt lethargic and tired the first time she took it, so she only took a half dose the next time. She felt much better and she did not have the headaches or the "swishing" that started in her left ear. She feels like it is definitely helping but she does not know if it is not going to be okay until she stops drinking.

She is taking the full dose of hydrochlorothiazide. She denies chest tightness or shortness of breath. She is doing blood pressure checks at home. She reports that in the morning she is seeing lower numbers than in the evening. Her readings are ranging from 130 to 145/95 to 100. She states that in the evenings if she sits there for a while and then takes it, it goes down. Kind of like when she comes here, it is always high but then it goes down. In the mornings it is generally more normal where it is supposed to be. She is taking her medicine in the morning when she gets up instead of in the evening. It sounds like we are not too far out of where we want to be.

