• Medical Treatment: She would like to start naltrexone. We discussed this previously. She will take the injectable form and start on 5/17/2021. We reviewed side effects and risks. The potential benefit of alcohol cessation would be highly beneficial to her for many reasons. Hypertension, she is taking lisinopril 10 mg daily and hydrochlorothiazide 12.5 mg daily. Quite possibly her blood pressure will improve completely with cessation of alcohol. Her target blood pressure is 130/140.
• Patient Education and Counseling: We discussed the benefits of alcohol cessation. I advised her that her blood pressure will likely improve with cessation of alcohol.
