Left elbow x-ray: No evidence of fracture.

Endoscopy: Episodic gastritis.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Left elbow pain.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient presents with left elbow pain. She is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease. The patient reports that she sits at her desk for work and types a lot. On physical examination, there is erythema and edema of the left elbow, pain to palpation of the left olecranon, and warmth to palpation. There is pain with flexion and extension of the left elbow. The left radial pulse is palpable.
• Medical Treatment: I advised the patient to ice the area and to get a little pillow for her elbow. She will take meloxicam 15 mg once a day. She will also continue to use her current Keppra 500 mg twice a day.

Epilepsy.
