PHYSICAL EXAM

Neurological
- Motor: Normal strength in all extremities.
- Sensation: Normal sensation in all extremities.
- Reflexes: Normal reflexes in all extremities.
- DTR: Normal DTR in all extremities.
- Gait: Normal gait. No antalgic gait.
- Spine: Examination of the spine shows no tenderness to palpation of the lumbar spine. No focal neurological deficits.

RESULTS

X-rays of the lumbar spine obtained today show no evidence of compression fractures.

ASSESSMENT

- Lumbar strain.

PLAN

- Medical Reasoning: The patient had an injury to her back when she was twisting at the birthday party. She does not have any pain or numbness in her legs. She has some stiffness with rotation but no evidence of a pinched nerve. She has a history of lumbar fusion. She does not have any other significant medical problems.
- Medical Treatment: I have recommended that she continue to take Motrin 800 mg three times a day with food. I have advised her to use ice and heat alternating on her back. I have recommended that she walk. She should return if it is not improving or worsening over the next week.
