summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Evaluation for high blood sugar.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Hannah Garcia is a 52-year-old female who presents for evaluation of high blood sugar. The patient states that she has been eating a lot of sweets recently due to the holidays and she felt fine initially but has started to feel lightheaded and dizzy over the past week. She was seen in the emergency room and she was treated with intravenous fluids and advised to cut out extra sweets and get back into her normal routine. She is having difficulty following this advice due to being around a lot of baked goods at home. She denies fever, chills, chest pain, shortness of breath, abdominal pain, or burning with urination. She does have osteoarthritis and endorses joint pain but denies any other joint pain or muscle aches. She has a history of atrial fibrillation and denies palpitations outside of anxiety. She denies any recent chest pain or palpitations. She states she is doing well with her reflux and is currently taking Protonix 40 mg once a day.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Constitutional: Denies fever or chills.
• Cardiovascular: Denies chest pain or shortness of breath. Denies palpitations outside of anxiety.
• Gastrointestinal: Denies abdominal pain. Denies burning with urination.
• Musculoskeletal: Denies joint pain other than osteoarthritis.
• Neurological: Denies headaches, dizziness, or visual changes.

PHYSICAL EXAMINATION

• Constitutional: Appears well.
• Neck: Thyroid is a little bit enlarged, but non-tender.
• Heart: Irregular rate and rhythm.
• Pulmonary: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.
• Abdomen: Soft, no tenderness, no hepatosplenomegaly.
• Extremities: No edema in the lower extremities.

RESULTS

Blood glucose: Elevated.
Hemoglobin A1c: Elevated.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Hannah Garcia is a 52-year-old female who presents for evaluation of high blood sugar. She has a history of atrial fibrillation and osteoarthritis.

Diabetes Mellitus, Type Unknown.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient has elevated blood glucose and hemoglobin A1c.
• Medical Treatment: I have ordered a complete metabolic panel to evaluate for type 1 or type 2 diabetes. I have also prescribed metformin 500 mg twice a day to help keep her blood sugar down.

Atrial Fibrillation.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient is in atrial fibrillation.
• Medical Treatment: We will continue her on metoprolol 25 mg twice a day.

Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient is doing well with her Protonix.
• Medical Treatment: Continue Protonix 40 mg once a day.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up with me in 2 weeks to review her blood sugar levels and the results of her autoimmune labs. }}<|eot_id|>
