EKG is unremarkable.

ASSESSMENT

1. Unstable angina.
2. Diabetes mellitus.
3. Hypertension.

PLAN

The patient was seen today for the evaluation of chest pain. She reports that the onset of the chest pain began approximately 3 months ago. The pain is alleviated when she stops walking. She denies any chest pain at this time. She denies shortness of breath, sweating, or diaphoresis. She denies any chest pain radiating to other areas. She denies nausea, vomiting, or abdominal pain. She denies any dizziness or syncope. She denies any dyspnea, wheezing, or cough. She denies any hemoptysis. She denies any chest pain with exertion.

Given her history of diabetes and suspected history of hypertension, I am concerned that she may be having an unstable angina. I have reviewed her EKG, which is unremarkable. I have also reviewed her vitals, which are within normal limits. I have also reviewed her exam, which is unremarkable except for her 2/6 systolic ejection murmur and 1+ non-pitting edema in the lower extremities.

I have ordered a cardiac stress test to be performed.

I have also prescribed the patient nitroglycerin 0.4 mg sublingual every 5 minutes PRN for chest pain.

I have also advised the patient to contact the emergency room if her chest pain persists after taking the nitroglycerin.

The patient will follow up with cardiology in one week.

The patient will follow up with me in two weeks.

The patient will also follow up with ophthalmology in two weeks for her diabetic retinopathy.

She will continue metformin 500 mg twice daily.

She will use a blood pressure cuff at home and enter her findings into Epic MyChart. I will get a reading of those as well. When she comes back in two weeks, we will keep a log of her blood pressure daily in the morning when she wakes up and see how things are going and then if we need to make any adjustments to the medications we can. I have also prescribed the patient hydrochlorothiazide 25 mg once daily for her hypertension.

Patient education was provided regarding the use of nitroglycerin. She was also provided with a handout regarding the side effects of hydrochlorothiazide. }}<|eot_id|>
