Osteoarthritis: The patient reports that her osteoarthritis has been flaring up a little bit lately, so she wants to talk about that primarily. She states that it is mostly in her elbows and it has been bothering her. She has been sitting at the computer at the desk more in the office, so she does not know if it is being stagnant in that position all day has increased flare-ups for that, but she wanted to talk to the doctor about that. She is right-handed. She denies any other joint pain. She denies any numbing or tingling in her hands. She states that she sometimes feels a little bit of numbing when she is typing for long periods of time, and she tries to shake out her arms a little bit to relieve that sensation. We will order an x-ray of her right elbow. We will prescribe meloxicam 15 mg once a day for the pain and the swelling. We will see how the x-ray shows up and the results of that before we refer her for any type of physical therapy.

Psoriasis: The patient reports that she has been under control. She reports that she is doing a lot better with the clobetasol for her scalp. She is stable. We will continue her on the steroid cream for her scalp.

