Neurological: Gait testing using the Tinetti assessment tool: Gait score 6/8, balance score 12/16, total score 18/28. Cranial nerves: Pupils are equal. Extraocular movements are intact. Face is symmetric. No dysarthria. Motor: Normal bulk and strength. Coordination slow from finger to nose.
Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.

RESULTS

CT of the head on 10/15/2020 shows a frontal horn span at the level of the foramen of Monro of 4.6 cm with a third ventricular contour that is flat with a span of 10 mm. There is a tiny amount of blood in the right frontal region with a tiny subdural collection. This was not noticed or noted by the radiologist who stated any extra-axial fluid collections. There is also small vessel ischemic change.

ASSESSMENT

Adult hydrocephalus.

PLAN

We will continue to monitor the patient's improvement in his gait and cognitive function. The patient will follow up in 3 months.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up in 3 months. }}<|eot_id|>
